<title>USA: RJR Nabisco says no comment on LeBow's slate.</title>
<headline>RJR Nabisco says no comment on LeBow's slate.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>RJR Nabisco Holdings Corp said on Tuesday it has been notified of a slate of nominees to the company's board put forward by Bennett LeBow but does not consider his action worthy of comment.</p>
<p>&quot;RJR Nabisco said LeBow's action did not merit additional comment,&quot; the company said in a written release.</p>
<p>The company was responding to news that LeBow, the chairman of Brooke Group, would nominate a slate of candidates to stand for election to the board of directors at RJR's annual meeting in April, 1997.  </p>
<p>The nominees, which include LeBow, support an immediate spin-off of the 80.5 percent-owned Nabisco Holdings Corp subsidiary from RJR's tobacco business.</p>
</text>
